 the untimed path is real but the temporal constraint is untested, and rather than 'absent' because nothing I observed rules the cascade out. Resolving this needs a time-filtered edge or event-listing tool for the three hops above.", "narrative_note": "Decision driven by absence of timestamp-resolving tools, not by negative temporal evidence."}, "raw_final_response": "I have exhausted my budget. Notably, **none of the available tools expose timestamps** \u2014 every result was aggregated over the full horizon [0, 100000], so I could never test the ordering or the \u2264600-unit gap constraint that defines the cascade.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_30df0d06\",\n  \"decision\": \"insufficient\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1006, 1860, 45, 153, 1680],\n  \"window\": [18031, 56431],\n  \"confidence\": 0.34,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Static reachability from 1006 to 1860 exists: 1006 emits to 6 targets (step_03), 1860 receives from 9 sources (step_04), and two 3-hop chains close the gap \u2014 1006->45->153->1860 and 1006->1680->153->1860 (step_05, step_07, step_08, step_09, step_10). The other four out-neighbours of 1006 (230, 698, 925, 475) do not reach 1860's in-neighbourhood {153,182,406,464,618,829,958,1390,1887} in one hop except 475->618 (steps 11-14), so the candidate routes are few and all funnel through hubs. That funnelling is the core problem: 153 (334 events, 253 partners) and 274 (562 events, 395 partners) are top-5 hubs graph-wide (step_15, step_16), so a static path through them is essentially guaranteed by popularity alone and is not evidence of influence transfer. Critically, every tool available to me aggregates over the full horizon [0,100000] (step_01) and returns no event times: I could not check whether the 1006->45, 45->153 and 153->1860 events fall inside [18031,56431], whether they occur in increasing order, or whether consecutive hops are separated by at most 600 units. Each of these edges fires exactly once (step_07, step_08, step_09), so the chain is a single fragile ordering with no repeat attempts to fall back on, and with a 600-unit budget against a 100000-unit horizon the prior that three specific one-shot events line up correctly is low. I therefore report 'insufficient' rather than 'present': the untimed path is real but the temporal constraint is untested, and rather than 'absent' because nothing I observed rules the cascade out. Resolving this needs a time-filtered edge or event-listing tool for the three hops above.\",\n  \"narrative_note\": \"Decision driven by absence of timestamp-resolving tools, not by negative temporal evidence.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 29977, "total_output_tokens": 4603, "total_tokens": 34580, "total_latency_ms": 63898, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}